<%# Name, feed, state, count, and the way off the roster.

    Removing is a button rather than a link, because it is a DELETE — see
    .claude/rules/views.md — and it confirms, because it is the one
    irreversible cascade in this app: the posts go, and so do the citations in
    published editions naming them.

    The button carries its own accessible name. Every row's says "Remove", so
    a reader who cannot see which row they are in has nothing to tell three
    of them apart. %>
<li class="pen__item pen__item--source">
  <span class="sources__name"><%= row.name %></span>
  <% if row.feed? %>
    <span class="sources__feed"><%= row.feed_url %></span>
  <% end %>
  <span class="<%= row.state_class %>"><%= row.state %></span>
  <span class="sources__count"><%= row.count %></span>
  <%= button_to t(".remove"), blog_path(row), method: :delete,
        class: "sources__remove", form_class: "sources__remove-form",
        aria: { label: t(".remove_blog", name: row.name) },
        data: { turbo_confirm: t(".confirm", name: row.name) } %>
</li>
